<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="bg-canvas py-20 px-6 md:px-8">
  <div class="max-w-[640px] mx-auto">
    <h2 class="font-serif font-normal text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.15] mb-8 text-ink">Questions families ask</h2>

    <div class="divide-y divide-hair">

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Isn't this the same as making a will?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No, but it complements one. Collator helps you organise the information a will, or a family, would need: what exists, where it's kept, and who's involved. For drafting or updating a will itself, speak to a qualified lawyer.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">How do we even start this conversation with my parents?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          Try framing it as "let's make sure we know where things are," not "let's plan for the worst." Many families start with something low-stakes, like insurance policies or property papers, and go from there.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">What if my parents don't want to share everything with me?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          They don't have to. The vault lives on their device, and they choose what, if anything, to share, and with whom. Collator doesn't require a shared account.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-4">
        <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span class="text-ink text-[.9375rem] font-medium">Is any of this shared with you, or with anyone else?</span>
          {% icon "chevron-down", "w-4 h-4 text-muted shrink-0 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" %}
        </summary>
        <p class="text-dim text-[.9375rem] leading-relaxed opacity-80 mt-3">
          No. Everything stays on the device it's entered on, and in your own backup if you enable one. Read more on our <a href="/privacy" class="text-saffron hover:text-saffron-deep transition-colors">privacy page</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

